NAME
        bal asyncapi http - Generate Ballerina source files from an AsyncAPI
                            definition for HTTP/Webhook protocols

SYNOPSIS
        bal asyncapi http -i <asyncapi-definition-file-path>
                         [-o <output-directory>]
                         [--module <module-name>]
                         [--license <license-file-path>]

DESCRIPTION
        Generates Ballerina source files from an AsyncAPI definition
        file for HTTP Webhook protocol integrations.

        The --input flag is mandatory. All other flags are optional.

        The output directory must be a Ballerina package. If a --module flag is provided, the
        generated files are written into the modules/<module-name>/
        directory of that package, making them a proper Ballerina module
        that compiles as part of the package. If no --module flag is
        given, the generated files are written directly into the root of
        the package.

OPTIONS
        -i, --input <asyncapi-definition-file-path>
                This is a mandatory input. The path to the AsyncAPI
                definition file (.yaml, .yml, or .json).

        -o, --output <output-directory>
                This is an optional input. The path to the target
                output directory for the generated Ballerina files.
                If not given, defaults to the current working directory.
                It should be a ballerina package.

        --module <module-name>
                This is an optional input. The name of the Ballerina
                module to generate code into. The module name must
                be a valid Ballerina identifier and must not exceed 256
                characters.

        --license <license-file-path>
                This is an optional input. The path to a file
                containing the license header to be added to all
                generated Ballerina files.

        -h, --help
                Display help for the http subcommand.

EXAMPLES
        Generate Ballerina files from an AsyncAPI definition in the
        current directory.

            $ bal asyncapi http -i definition.yaml

        Generate Ballerina files into a specific Ballerina package.

            $ bal asyncapi http -i definition.yaml \
                                -o ./myproject

        Generate Ballerina files into a specific module inside a
        Ballerina package.

            $ bal asyncapi http -i definition.yaml \
                                --module payments

        Generate Ballerina files into a specific output directory
        with a license header.

            $ bal asyncapi http -i definition.yaml \
                                -o ./myproject \
                                --license license.txt
